+# Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+Status: implemented. Normative contract: `specs/state.md`
+("Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile").
+
+## Approach
+
+Eligible compiler-generated `pure_projection` steps persist only an exact
+value-free completion shell; resume re-derives needed values in memory.
+
+- `orchestrator/workflow/pure_result_replay_index.py` derives eligibility and
+  dependencies from the loaded bundle (control-flow cycles and loop ownership
+  are multiply visited; lineage-bearing nodes are ineligible).
+- `orchestrator/workflow/pure_result_replay.py` owns the shell, the progress
+  classifier and the leaf mutations behind the four `StateManager` visit
+  transactions (also exposed on call-frame managers).
+- `orchestrator/workflow/pure_result_replay_runtime.py` (`PureReplayRuntime`)
+  audits leaves and persisted surfaces, replays nodes into a process-local
+  cache, and overlays reconstructed values on the in-memory state only.
+- `orchestrator/workflow/pure_replay_executor.py` composes the runtime into
+  `WorkflowExecutor`: pre-prologue audit, replay after the single restart
+  determination, eligible visit begin/settle, no result bundle for eligible
+  nodes.
+- Checkpoints: eligible pure points emit no record and contribute no restore
+  binding; default resume filters them before nearest-boundary selection and
+  admits one zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- Keeping value rows but dropping bundles only: still trusts persisted copies of
+  derivable values, so rejected.
+- Replaying every completed eligible node on resume: simpler, but fails closed
+  for values nothing downstream needs; replay is seeded from the remaining
+  program's references and the workflow outputs instead.
+- Inferring the profile from the parent frame or path suffix: rejected; the
+  callee's typed provenance alone selects it.
+
+## Makes harder
+
+- Dashboards or tools reading `steps.<pure>.artifacts` from `state.json` see
+  shells; they must use workflow outputs or the in-memory result.
+- Progress classification is strict, so hand-edited pure rows fail closed.
