+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile
+
+The additive root/call-frame state field `result_persistence_profile` selects how
+compiler-generated `pure_projection` results persist. State schema stays `2.1`.
+
+- Selector
+  - Absent: historical bundle-backed persistence; `to_dict()` omits the key and `from_dict()` of a payload without it yields `None` and round-trips unchanged.
+  - The only supported present value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`. Any other value fails closed with a `ValueError` naming the profile at `RunState` construction, `StateManager.initialize(...)`, and state load. A failed load never rewrites the state file.
+  - `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)` writes the field atomically with the initial state, before any visit. Ordinary loads never infer, backfill, or upgrade the field.
+  - Automatic selection: a compiled `.orc` run (`orchestrator run`), a new root created by `orchestrator resume --force-restart` (the source run is left byte-for-byte unchanged), and a fresh non-iterative call frame whose callee bundle has validated provenance `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"`. The callee's typed provenance alone decides; the parent's profile, path suffix, alias, or step identity never do. A fresh retry after a failed non-iterative Workflow Lisp predecessor is new state and selects the profile.
+  - Existing roots and frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees, and iteration-owned child frames keep the historical profile. An existing frame is never backfilled; a malformed one (no `state`, or a non-mapping `state`) is rejected with a `ValueError` mentioning `existing call-frame state` before anything is written.
+
+- Eligibility
+  - A pure node is replay-eligible when it is compiler-generated, acyclic, visited at most once per scope, and carries no `publishes`/`consumes` lineage. Recurrent, loop-owned, and other multiply visited pure nodes are ineligible (`multiple_visit_region`) and keep full durable rows, bundles, and checkpoints inside a profiled root.
+  - Refs are scoped to the workflow that holds them; an imported callee indexes only its own nodes under its own scope `root`. Only exact `{"ref": ...}` leaves form dependencies, and every literal subtree must match its declared binding type.
+
+- Value-free completion shell
+  - An eligible success persists exactly `{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0, "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed", "retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}`; any extra key (`value`, `output`, `text`, `json`, `artifacts`, `debug`, `duration_ms`, `output_bundle`, ...), missing key, or wrong value is invalid. Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows.
+  - No pure result bundle, private lineage entry, lexical checkpoint record, or restore binding is written for an eligible node; checkpoint records are still written for effect boundaries.
+  - The visit is one atomic transaction pair: `begin_eligible_pure_visit` increments the visit and publishes the running cursor; settlement persists the shell (or the full failed/skipped row) and clears the cursor.
+  - Progress classification per visit is `unstarted`, `interrupted` (visit plus matching cursor), `derived_complete` (visit plus exact shell), `durable_failure_skip`, or `progress_witness_invalid` for any other combination (for example a visit-two cursor or shell, cursor plus row, or a value-bearing completion).
+
+- Resume
+  - Resume re-derives the needed pure values in memory from durable inputs and earlier durable results. Replay never dispatches an effect, increments a visit, settles a result, or writes durable state; reconstructed values live only in the process-local overlay of the in-memory state.
+  - A persisted value row, pure bundle, or private-lineage entry for an eligible node, or a checkpoint record or restore binding for it in the same scope, is a `profile_conflict` raised before the prologue or any state write.
+  - Failures before any effect use `error.type: "pure_result_replay_unavailable"` with `error.context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`, `progress_witness_invalid`.
+  - Default resume admits exactly one zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (`selection_reason: validated_frame_entry_replay`, `checkpoint_id: null`), when no durable prior boundary exists and the profile, progress witnesses, and bound-input leaves validate; otherwise it fails closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`. Replay-eligible pure points are filtered out of the durable checkpoint candidates before unique-nearest selection, and selection never scans past an invalid nearest durable boundary.
+  - A resume determines the restart boundary exactly once and passes it to the default-resume decision.
+
 ## State File Schema (example)
 
 The state file (`${RUN_ROOT}/state.json`) is the authoritative record of execution:
